  "comparability": "Redis 8 与 ling 的有界、交错、闭环对照；Bounded interleaved Redis 8 / ling comparison.\n\nLinux only; starts private child processes, never attaches to an existing service.\nGET / SET / SET PX use equal keys, payload bytes, connections and pipeline depth 1.\nFast retains ling events while Redis disables persistence. Reliable journals events;\nRedis AOF always persists values and may group parallel commands into one fsync.\nThese durability objects are different: report each pair separately, never one ranking.\nThe shared Python process, protocol codecs and same-host CPU budget limit this workload.\nRedis core retains its bundled vectorset module; no external modules are accepted.\n",
  "audit_scope": "Raw successful request latencies only; client CPU has no recorded endpoints to independently recompute. RSS endpoints and lifetime VmHWM include preload/warmup. Frozen input bytes match independently supplied pins; recorded revision/version metadata must agree, but archive hash alone does not prove binary build provenance. No executable is run.",
  "limitations": [
    "Pre-release closed-loop same-host comparison of ling 0.2.0 and the pinned Redis build; no 0.3.0 release or post-release acceptance is implied.",
    "Fast persistence and Reliable durability objects differ; report each system/scenario separately, never a single overall ranking.",
    "CPU values, RSS endpoints and lifetime VmHWM retain the original measurement boundaries; no continuous peaks, saturation, leak absence or endurance claim.",
    "Official source and successful build records bind recorded inputs; this archiver does not independently reproduce the build.",
    "Windows copies preserve file bytes, not original Linux owner/mode metadata. No WSL, tests, builds, analyzer or load is started by this script."
